
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:image@

%9Parameters:%9

    ON:         Enables image preview (sets image_preview ON).
    OFF:        Disables image preview, cancels running downloads and
                forgets the previews of all lines.
    CLEAR:      Deletes the cached images and forgets the previews of all
                lines.
    STATS:      Displays the cache directory, the number of cached files,
                their total size, and the cache hits and misses.

    Without any parameter, a short usage text is displayed.

%9Description:%9

    Controls the image preview, which shows a picture linked in a line in a
    popup drawn inside the terminal. It is available when erssi is built with
    image preview support (libcurl and chafa).

    Click a line with the left mouse button to preview an image link in it.
    Recognised links are http and https URLs ending in .jpg, .jpeg, .png,
    .gif or .webp, i.imgur.com and i.ibb.co links, and imgur.com, ibb.co and
    kermit.pw pages, whose image is taken from the page. The image is
    downloaded in the background and shown when it is ready; a click or
    most key presses close the popup.

    A link is someone else's URL, so it may only lead to a public web
    server over http or https: addresses of this host and of local
    networks are refused, also after a redirect. A download stops at
    image_preview_max_file_size even when the server does not announce the
    size, or sends less than 1 KB/s for 15 seconds. Images larger than 8192
    pixels on a side or 40 megapixels are not shown.

    Downloaded images are kept in the image_cache directory inside the
    configuration directory. The file of a shown image is deleted again 30
    seconds after it was displayed, and files older than 7 days are removed.

    Settings:

        image_preview (default: ON)
            Enables the preview.
        image_preview_blitter (default: auto)
            How the image is drawn: kitty, iterm2, sixel or symbols (text
            characters). 'auto' detects the terminal, also through tmux.
        image_preview_max_width, image_preview_max_height (default: 0)
            The largest popup size in columns and lines; 0 uses 80%% of the
            window.
        image_preview_max_bytes (default: 2000000)
            The largest size of the drawn image data; larger images are
            scaled down.
        image_preview_max_file_size (default: 10)
            The largest image to download, in megabytes.
        image_preview_timeout (default: 60s)
            The time limit of a download.
        image_preview_cache_size (default: 100M)
            The intended largest size of the cache. Going over it only
            logs a warning; no files are removed for it.
        image_preview_debug (default: OFF)
            Writes a debug log, including every clicked URL, to
            image-preview-debug.log in the configuration directory.

%9Examples:%9

    /IMAGE ON
    /IMAGE STATS
    /IMAGE CLEAR
    /SET image_preview_blitter sixel
    /SET image_preview_max_file_size 5

%9See also:%9 SET

